# Herdr writes its runtime state alongside its config: sockets, logs, session
# snapshots, plugin and release-note caches. Only config.toml belongs in version
# control. Stow never links this file into $HOME -- \.gitignore is in its
# default ignore list -- so this is repo-side protection only; the real defence
# is the mkdir in bootstrap.sh that stops stow folding ~/.config/herdr.
*
!.gitignore
!config.toml
